620-IAC-1-1-30", "kind": "summary", "text": "Indiana adopts the federal excavation rule, 29 CFR 1926.650 through 1926.652 with Appendices A to F, by reference (620 IAC 1-1-30, items 7 and 18; effective in Indiana March 5, 1990). So a trench 5 feet or deeper needs a protective system (sloping, benching, shoring or a shield) unless it is entirely in stable rock, and a competent person inspects daily (29 CFR 1926.652(a)(1), 1926.651(k)). The adopting rule shows no Indiana depth, permit or other excavation requirement of its own. OSHA's Indiana state plan page lists a unique excavation standard; it was not identified, so ask IOSHA if a job depends on it (not confirmed).", "tier": "core", "state": "IN", "title": "Indiana trench protection: IOSHA adopts the federal excavation rule, 5 feet", "topic": "State safety plan: trench and excavation", "source": "620 IAC 1-1-30 (adoption by reference from 54 FR, 29 CFR 1926 Subpart P)", "checked": "2026-11-20", "edition": "620 IAC 1-1-30 as posted, read 2026-11-20", "license": "gov-state", "confidence": "medium", "unconfirmed": "yes"}]]$kb$::jsonb) e;
